      "side": 1,
      "message": "Naming things. We don\u0027t have a good name for these `-1` or `/dev/null` values. The idea is that they greatly simplify the rest of the code in that you can keep using them, they just don\u0027t actually add anything to the document. It\u0027s not even so much that this Mark is default or empty but that it isn\u0027t hooked up to anything and so anything written to it will just \"go away\" instead of be kept around in the set of marks on pages of the document. So maybe a better term would be \"unattached\" or \"detached\" (English has many words). Or maybe just more words here.",
